\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Eternal beam Of Light Divine,
\par Fountain of unexhausted love,
\par In whom the Father's glories shine
\par Through earth beneath and heaven above.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Jesu's the weary wanderer's rest,
\par Give me Thy easy yoke to bear,
\par With steadfast patience arm my breast,
\par With spotless love and lowly fear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thankful I take the cup from Thee,
\par Prepared and mingled by Thy skill,
\par Though bitter to the taste it be,
\par Powerful the wounded soul to heal.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Be Thou, O Rock of Ages, nigh!
\par So shall each murmuring thought be gone,
\par And grief, and fear, and care shall fly,
\par As clouds before the midday sun.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Speak to my warring passions:Peace!
\par Say to my trembling heart: Be still!
\par Thy power my strength and fortress is,
\par For all things serve Thy sovereign will.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. O death! Where is thy sting?Where now
\par Thy boasted victory, O grave?
\par Who shall contend with God? Or who
\par Can hurt whom God delights to save?\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

